  <teiHeader>
    <fileDesc>
      <titleStmt>
        <title>Mahāvyutpatti - DDBC version</title>
      </titleStmt>
      <publicationStmt>
        <p>This digital edition of the Mahāvyutpatti was created by the Glossaries Team at Dharma
          Drum Buddhist College (法鼓佛教學院), Taiwan.</p>
        <p>See http://buddhistinformatics.ddbc.edu.tw/glossaries/ or email glossaries@ddbc.edu.tw
          for more information.</p>
      </publicationStmt>
      <sourceDesc>
        <p>The Mahāvyutpatti (bye brag rtog byed) was first compiled in the early 9th century as a
          glossary to aid the translation of Sanskrit Buddhist scriptures into Tibetan. Later
          Chinese, Mongolian and Manchu equivalents were added. This version contains Sanskrit,
          Tibetan and Chinese.</p>
      </sourceDesc>
    </fileDesc>
